          "import_seq": 15001,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "Lessons from Matt 25\n\n• Not how much you have but what you do with what you have.\n\n• Likes not Liars - Deal with it. - Multiply what you get.\n\n• God expects us to increase what he's given.\n\n• Obstacles\n  • Fear that God was harsh - know God will meet you\n  • In Comparison of wealthy - Don't judge others.\n  • Protecting from loss is good enough - Stewardship - Bless others\n  • know God is for you. Expect him to bless you on Jesus\n  • Don't compare \u0026 judge. Steward's celebrate\n  • Not losing isn't winning. Invest.\n  • Starting amount is not what we are judged on, it's what we did with what we were given. How do we steward\n  What do we steward - Time Talent Treasure\n\nTime/Attention - Talent - Treasure\n\nMake Money =\n\nManage - Budgeting\n\nMobilizing - Investing\n\nMultiplying - Scaling\n\nIntro - Ram (great employer/friend)\n- Share tips \u0026 tricks. Preacher not Marketplace guru.\n- Expectations.\n- Management \u003e Making - Compound interest\n- Understand money = Time \u0026 Energy\n  • House in 2001 150k, 900k = 6x    4x now\n    35k  45k = 1.85x\n\n- Make \u0026 ask\n- Manage\n- Mobilise\n- Multiply\n\nMatt 25 - Not how much we have\n         what we do with what we have\n  • Called to steward - time talent treasure\n  • No fear\n  • No comparison\n  • No judging\n  • No laziness\n  • No failure\n\nMale                Mind - Imagination\n              Mouth - Network Mentoring\n                      Manage Marketing\n      muscle",
