          "journal_date": "2025-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "Tuesday 1 \u0026 Wednesday 2\n\nJackson 1 did drop in + he did drop out.\n\nMarcus is dropping out in a few weeks. He's saddening; GRE/editing S-state is taking all his time \u0026 he can't do everything.\n\nEditing corrections - IRE directs different in different edits. I need to see if he's changing it on purpose or by accident.\n\nEdit note: Consistency of definite article use in definitions like \"the IRE\" vs \"an IRE\". Track usages. Does he use \"the\" as a default pattern? Is it meaningful?\n\nO - details - Small issues - Examples - Same language - Small examples - Same language as in examples. E.g. all - same - Bracket issue. Numbers 2.2.3 etc.\n\nOK so hold these - Same language as main brackets. Like other - examples - the Same language as in examples = Brackets \"8.2.3\" etc.\n\nA - The bracket from like is the (IRE) reference to the def'ns of a \"State\" referred to in prior - previous work in Bracket D.\n\nP - Good refuge - be justified our prior work definitions and add the brackets\n\nS - I found be to add all brackets before I became weary about the work. I need to find new more evidence in A+ more.\n\nS - I God in to all that could help. I notice that God all help\n\nS-L 2",
