        {
          "created_at": "2026-07-05T01:35:40.887667+00:00",
          "date_precision": "year",
          "date_reviewed": true,
          "id": "362ab7c3-192d-42db-806a-f91753d8a37a",
          "import_batch_id": "b6b1042e-bed6-40e2-80f4-debdd9e59219",
          "import_seq": 2003,
          "journal_date": "2025-01-01",
          "ocr_text": "Observation: This passage talks about walking in light vs darkness, \u0026 the importance of confession. It emphasizes that God is light \u0026 there is no darkness in Him. Those who claim to have fellowship with God but walk in darkness are liars. We must walk in the light. If we confess our sins, God will forgive us \u0026 cleanse us. The promise is conditional on confession. Application: I need to examine my life. Am I walking in the light or darkness? Do I confess my sins regularly? I should not deceive myself about my sin. I should be quick to confess \u0026 repent. God is faithful to forgive when I confess. Prayer: Lord, help me to walk in the light. Show me any areas of darkness in my life. Give me the courage to confess my sins. Thank You for Your faithfulness to forgive \u0026 cleanse me. In Jesus' name, Amen.\n\n3. Be a whole person\n\nDevelop other areas of life\n\n[Diagram showing: Pastor, Investor, Father, Husband]\n\nDraining                    Neutral                    Replenishing\n\nI'm not what I do, have or what others think, but what God thinks and He thinks I'm His Beloved.\n\nOWN Feelings.  Observe\n                     Write\n                     Navigate\n\nThere is a pain-joy faucet that always is easy on Reservoir—Jesus is always with us. But what activity allows you to experience the manifest presence of God.\n\nJohn Ortberg\n12 steps of AA. Framework of Spiritual Growth.\nRoland H. Alcoholic Anonymous met Carl Jung.\n(Only hope is profound religious experience.\nOxford group→ Discipleship group → Alcoholics Anonymous → EBIT.→ Bill v→ Big Dad offshoot of Oxford Group\nAlcohol → Spirits → Don't be drunk with wine but w/ Spirit.\nAddiction is a desire of the Spirit.\nAddiction is a result many people in pain \u0026 suffering\n\n1. Powerless                    VISION, INTENSION, METHOD\n2. Believe in greater power    12 steps → In past tense\n3. Turn lives and will to God\n4. Take moral inventory",
          "person_id": "2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd",
          "photo_url": "https://yddjlhdptsundeimugba.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/soap-photos/2aa35958-9057-44bd-aaf2-bd12a4cf9ecd/1783212266236.jpeg",
